- Retain20k after game28 B+6: four wins, nineteen losses and one draw. Read game-028.md and game-027.md. Game28's surviving left23/right11 were alive but insufficient; seven dead White stones remained displayed.
- Build a viable second base before contact responses consume the endpoint turns. Game28's conditional47 was arithmetic, not secured ownership: the upper base never made an eye. After H7/H8 and D9, six stones only had G9; W G9, B H9 captures seven immediately. Earlier alternatives remain unverified.
- Count explicit rows/coordinates around moves10–16, exclude enemy points, and track needed boundary turns. Seek a reduction margin beyond minimum45 Black/38 White at an81-point split. Revise room AND viability when a route closes; recognizing a deficit must change development while space remains.
- Preserve B7/C6 same-color shared-eye life: B7 boundaries A7/B6/C7/B8; C6 boundaries B6/C5/C7/D6. Both White boundary groups retain the other eye on a Black fill, making it suicide. Do not fill these eyes for an unnecessary connection. A8 later joined both while preserving them.
- Rebuild after captures and make actual orthogonal connections. Game28 A7 captured three after an ignored atari, B6 connected the capturer, B4/B3 saved C3. Lower-right G2 joined F2/G3, E2 joined E1/F2, G1 captured F1 and made true F1; H1/J1 was a separate secured eye space.
- Check every threat's own liberties and the opponent's simplest connection. J4 was a safe atari, but H4 answered; J5 would leave two stones only J6 and allow immediate capture. Safe threats and ignored ataris do not establish forced gains.
- Before every move scan ALL own groups for atari/cuts, actual eyes, playable escape routes and largest area opportunity. Connected stones or current liberties do not prove life. Read beyond captures and check all neighbors before declaring an enemy stone isolated.
- Keep every returned position before continuing; save full SGF, result, reviews and replay evidence. Code is limited to inspection, legality and records, never move selection/search.
- Previous focus is in next-game-focus-through-027.md and earlier through-026/025/024/023 files. Keep game26's corrected B1/A2 opposing-color trap proof and game27's clean survival/count lessons.

`;
